<file path="backend/modules/rag/knowledge_base.txt">
# FitForge Knowledge Base

## General Rules
1. FitForge is an AI-powered fitness platform connecting users with professional trainers.
2. The AI Assistant (FitForge AI) is powered by Google Gemini and is available 24/7 to answer fitness questions.

## Diet Guidelines
3. For weight loss, a caloric deficit of 300-500 calories per day is recommended.
4. Protein intake should be around 1.6g to 2.2g per kilogram of body weight for muscle gain.
5. Hydration is key: Drink at least 3-4 liters of water daily, especially on workout days.
6. A standard healthy breakfast could include oats, eggs, and a piece of fruit. Puttu (a traditional Kerala dish) contains about 250-300 calories per serving depending on the coconut ratio.
7. Meal timing matters: consume a protein-rich meal within 30-60 minutes after a workout for optimal muscle recovery.
8. Avoid ultra-processed foods, excessive sugar, and trans fats. Focus on whole foods: vegetables, lean proteins, healthy fats, and complex carbohydrates.

## Workout Guidelines
9. Progressive overload is the gradual increase of stress placed upon the body during exercise training. It is the most important principle for muscle growth.
10. A beginner should train 3 to 4 days a week, focusing on full-body workouts or upper/lower splits.
11. Rest days are crucial. Muscles grow during rest, not during the workout. Aim for 7-9 hours of sleep.
12. Best exercises for weight loss include a mix of strength training (like squats, deadlifts) and cardio (HIIT, running).
13. Compound movements like squats, deadlifts, bench press, and overhead press give the most muscle activation and calorie burn per exercise.
14. HIIT (High-Intensity Interval Training): alternating between intense bursts and recovery periods. Example: 30 seconds sprint, 30 seconds walk, repeated 10 times.

## Troubleshooting
15. If you experience sharp joint pain during an exercise, stop immediately and consult a doctor or your FitForge trainer. Muscle soreness (DOMS) is normal 24-48 hours after a workout.
16. Plateau in weight loss: if stuck for more than 2 weeks, consider adjusting calorie intake, changing workout type, or doing a diet break for 1-2 weeks.

## About FitForge Platform
17. FitForge is a comprehensive fitness ecosystem that bridges the gap between fitness enthusiasts and professional trainers.
18. The platform offers three main roles: Client, Trainer, and Admin. There is also a Manager role that helps supervise trainers.
19. Users can book 1-on-1 or Group Video sessions with their assigned trainers directly through the platform — no Zoom or Google Meet needed.
20. FitForge offers subscription tiers: Free, Wellness, and Personal Training. Premium subscribers get full access to all AI features, unlimited diet plans, and live coaching sessions.
21. The founder and CEO of FitForge is Hilal Ahmed, a certified personal trainer and software developer passionate about making fitness coaching accessible to everyone.

## FitForge Unique Features
22. Food AI Image Analyzer: Users can upload a picture of their meal and the AI automatically calculates the macros (Calories, Protein, Carbs, Fats).
23. WebRTC Video Calling: FitForge has an in-built high-quality video calling system. Trainers and clients can join live workout sessions without any third-party app. It supports both 1-on-1 and group sessions.
24. Real-Time Chat: FitForge provides secure real-time messaging between trainers and clients, protected by JWT authentication and Socket.io.
25. Body Transformation Predictor: Uses Gemini Vision AI and Stability AI to analyze a user's current physique and generate realistic transformation previews at 3 months, 6 months, and 1 year timelines.
26. AI Diet Plan Generator: Creates personalized diet plans based on the user's BMR, body measurements, country, and goal. Uses the US Navy Body Fat formula for accurate analysis.
27. Progress Tracker: Users can log their body weight, measurements, and workouts over time. FitForge charts this data visually so both clients and trainers can monitor improvement.
28. AI Fitness Chatbot: A RAG-powered AI assistant that can answer fitness, diet, and platform questions 24/7.

## Subscription & Pricing
29. FitForge Free Tier: access to the AI chatbot (rate limited), basic workout info, and a 1-day sample diet plan.
30. Wellness Plan: 7-day AI diet plan, unlimited Food AI scans, group video sessions, and real-time chat with a trainer.
31. Personal Training Plan: Everything in Wellness plus dedicated 1-on-1 live sessions, fully custom workout and diet plans, and direct real-time progress monitoring by the trainer.

## Trainer Guidelines
32. Trainers on FitForge are vetted professionals. They submit their certificates, specialties, and experience. The admin reviews and approves before they can take clients.
33. If a client misses a video session, the trainer can reschedule it or send a message via the built-in chat.
34. Trainer earnings are tracked through the platform. Payouts are managed by the FitForge admin panel.
35. Trainers can build custom workout plans and assign them to clients. They can also monitor client progress from their dashboard.

## Fitness & Nutrition Science
36. BMR (Basal Metabolic Rate): the calories your body burns at rest. FitForge uses the Mifflin-St Jeor formula: Men: (10 x weight kg) + (6.25 x height cm) - (5 x age) + 5. Women: (10 x weight kg) + (6.25 x height cm) - (5 x age) - 161.
37. TDEE (Total Daily Energy Expenditure) = BMR x Activity Multiplier. Sedentary=1.2, Light=1.375, Moderate=1.55, Very Active=1.725.
38. Macronutrients: Protein = 4 cal/gram, Carbohydrates = 4 cal/gram, Fat = 9 cal/gram.
39. Creatine monohydrate is one of the most researched supplements for strength and muscle gain. Standard dose: 3-5g per day.
40. Intermittent fasting (16:8 method) can be effective for fat loss but is not ideal for everyone, especially those focused on muscle building who need frequent protein intake.
41. US Navy Body Fat Formula (Men): 495 / (1.0324 - 0.19077 * log10(waist - neck) + 0.15456 * log10(height)) - 450.
42. Healthy body fat ranges: Men: 10-20% (fit), Women: 18-28% (fit). Above 25% for men or 35% for women is generally considered overweight.

## Live Database Context (Trainers)
